  abstract = {This paper concerns the asymptotic behavior of zeros and critical
points for monochromatic random waves $$ϕ
_λ $$of frequency $$λ $$on
a compact, smooth, Riemannian manifold (M, g) as
$$λ i̊ghtarrow
∈fty .$$We prove global variance estimates for the
measures of integration over the zeros and critical points of
$$ϕ _λ .$$These global
estimates hold for a wide class of manifolds---for example when
(M, g) has no conjugate points---and rely on new local variance
estimates on zeros and critical points of $$ϕ
_λ $$in balls of radius $$≈
λ ^\\-1\\$$around a fixed point. Our local
results hold under conditions about the structure of geodesics
that are generic in the space of all metrics on M.},
}

